3ccf","definition":"To extend the front of (a column), bringing it into line, deploy.","example":"The Englishmen[…]display their ranks and[…]press hard upon their enemies.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["characters","CRT","cursor","digits","graphics","monitor","screen","VDU"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/display#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:00174d6abc4070c012","definition":"To make conspicuous by using large or prominent type.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["characters","CRT","cursor","digits","graphics","monitor","screen","VDU"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/display#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:59e1471585bdd5844e","definition":"To discover; to descry.","example":"And from his seat took pleasure to display / The city so adorned with towers.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["characters","CRT","cursor","digits","graphics","monitor","screen","VDU"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/display#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f9e4e7f71c8e342c8a","definition":"To spread out, to unfurl.","example":"The wearie Traueiler, wandring that way, / Therein did often quench his thristy heat, / And then by it his wearie limbes display, / Whiles creeping slomber made him to forget / His former paine [...].","pos":"verb","synonyms":["splay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["characters","CRT","cursor","digits","graphics","monitor"